    "result_text": "The full test suite is green \u2014 **266 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**, BUILD SUCCESS.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change computes an owner's `initials` and returns them in the owner response. I followed the existing `displayName` computed-field pattern:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `initials` string field to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct `@Mapping` expression on `toOwnerDto` that computes the initials from the first letters of the first and last name, upper-cased and dot-separated with a trailing dot:\n   ```java\n   owner.getFirstName().substring(0, 1).toUpperCase() + \".\" +\n   owner.getLastName().substring(0, 1).toUpperCase() + \".\"\n   ```\n\nBecause the mapping lives in `toOwnerDto`, the field is populated on the create (POST) response as well as GET/list responses. The new `Cp07Tests.coreInitials` passes (`John` + last name starting with `S` \u2192 `J.S.`), and all pre-existing tests remain green.",
